# Password-gates the admin panel with a browser login prompt (HTTP Basic
# Auth) — a stopgap until the app has real in-app authentication of its
# own (see README.md's "Known follow-up").
#
# IMPORTANT: this only does anything if this app is actually served
# through Apache with AllowOverride enabled for this directory - e.g.
# traditional cPanel/shared hosting, or a VPS where Apache reverse-proxies
# to the Next.js process. Hosts like Vercel, Railway, Render or Netlify
# don't run Apache at all and will silently ignore this file entirely.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Run `npm run htpasswd -- <username>` here (from admin/) and follow the
#      prompt to create/update .htpasswd with a real, hashed password (see
#      README.md).
#   2. Replace AuthUserFile below with the ABSOLUTE filesystem path to that
#      .htpasswd on your actual server (Apache needs a real OS path here,
#      not a URL/relative path) - e.g. /home/youruser/public_html/admin/.htpasswd.

AuthType Basic
AuthName "Sayan Digital Admin"
AuthUserFile /REPLACE/WITH/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/admin/.htpasswd
Require valid-user
